B.bkc=new A.e9("How do I add my first property?","Tap the Properties tab at the bottom of the screen, then tap the + button in the top-right corner or the gold FAB. Fill in your property name, address, and optional photo, then tap Save. Your property will appear immediately in your dashboard.")
B.bk8=new A.e9("How do I invite a tenant to their unit?","Go to More \u2192 Invite Tenant (or tap the gold Invite Tenant tile). Select the vacant unit from the dropdown, enter your tenant's name, email address, and phone number, then tap Send Invitation. Your tenant will receive an email with a link to download Elevo and create their account.")
B.bkr=new A.e9("What is the Private Vault?","The Private Vault (More \u2192 Private Vault) is a landlord-only storage area for sensitive notes, private documents, screening results, and photos related to your units. Tenants can never see vault contents \u2014 even documents you upload there are completely hidden from tenant accounts.")
B.aXo=s([B.bkc,B.bk8,B.bkr],t.zX)
B.bk1=new A.hL("Getting Started",B.a65,B.aXo)
B.bke=new A.e9("How does per-property pricing work on Essential?","The Essential plan includes 1 property ($39.99/month or $299/year). Each additional property is $12.99/month. The Unlimited plan at $79/month covers unlimited properties.")
B.bkp=new A.e9("What is the Done-for-You setup add-on?","For a one-time fee of $249, the Elevo team will set up all your properties in the app, upload all your existing documents (leases, checklists, inspection reports), and configure your account settings. Ideal if you have multiple properties and want a clean start.")
B.bkn=new A.e9("How do I manage or cancel my subscription?","Go to More \u2192 Subscription & Pricing \u2192 Manage Subscription. This opens the Stripe Customer Portal where you can upgrade, downgrade, update your payment method, or cancel at any time. Changes take effect at the next billing cycle.")
B.bkh=new A.e9("How does the 7-day trial work?","Essential and Unlimited include a 7-day trial. A card is collected upfront and is charged when the trial ends unless you cancel first.")
B.aWz=s([B.bke,B.bkp,B.bkn,B.bkh],t.zX)
B.bjZ=new A.hL("Subscriptions & Billing",B.uI,B.aWz)
B.bk3=new A.e9("Does Elevo process rent payments?","No. Elevo is an information and record-keeping tool \u2014 it does not handle money. Rent is paid directly between tenant and landlord using your preferred method (Zelle, Venmo, bank transfer, check, or cash). Elevo records and tracks payment confirmations only.")
B.bkt=new A.e9("How do I enter my preferred payment methods?","Go to More \u2192 Payment Methods. Add each way you accept rent, such as Zelle, Venmo, check, or a bank transfer, with the handle and any instructions. Only your own tenants see them on their rent screen. You can edit, reorder, or remove a method later. Elevo does not collect the money.")
B.bkb=new A.e9("How does the tenant payment confirmation work?",'After a tenant pays you through their chosen method, they tap "I Have Paid" in the app. You receive a push notification and can review the payment record. Tap "Confirm Payment Received" to mark it as confirmed with a timestamp \u2014 this creates a permanent paper trail.')
B.aVG=s([B.bk3,B.bkt,B.bkb],t.zX)
B.bjT=new A.hL("Rent & Payments",B.es,B.aVG)
B.bkq=new A.e9("How does emergency maintenance work?","When a tenant submits a maintenance request with Emergency priority, Elevo immediately sends a push notification to your device \u2014 regardless of your notification preferences. Non-emergency requests also send a push notification and appear in your maintenance queue.")
B.bkl=new A.e9("What is vendor spend limit enforcement?","Each vendor in your directory has a spend limit (the max you authorize per job). When you assign a vendor to a maintenance request and enter an estimated cost at or below their limit, the vendor is notified automatically. If the estimate exceeds their limit, you receive an approval request first \u2014 the vendor is only notified after you approve.")
B.bk9=new A.e9("Can I track multiple vendors?","Yes \u2014 go to More \u2192 Vendors to manage your vendor directory. You can add unlimited vendors with contact info, trade category, and spend limits. Tap any vendor card to view their full profile, edit their information, or see their job history.")
B.aQF=s([B.bkq,B.bkl,B.bk9],t.zX)
B.bjV=new A.hL("Maintenance & Vendors",B.dR,B.aQF)
B.bkd=new A.e9("How long are documents stored?","Documents and photos are stored indefinitely in Supabase Storage as long as your Elevo subscription is active. Files are stored in private buckets with daily automatic backups. All download links expire after 1 hour for security \u2014 a new signed URL is generated each time you open a document.")
B.bk2=new A.e9("How do I generate a Move-Out Inspection Report?","Go to a unit's Photos tab (or More \u2192 Photo Log), select the Move-Out tab, and tap Generate Report. Elevo creates a PDF with side-by-side move-in and move-out photos, timestamps, and unit details that you can save or share directly.")
B.bkg=new A.e9("What does the P&L report include?","Go to More \u2192 Reports. You can view monthly or annual profit & loss. Income is automatically populated from confirmed rent payments. You can manually add expenses (repairs, HOA fees, insurance, taxes, etc.) and assign them to specific properties. The report shows net profit/loss, margin percentage, and an expense category breakdown.")
B.aV8=s([B.bkd,B.bk2,B.bkg],t.zX)
B.bk0=new A.hL("Documents & Reports",B.dq,B.aV8)
B.a67=new A.aC(62623,"Lucide","lucide_icons",!1)
B.bkm=new A.e9("How much can I charge for a security deposit in Arizona?","Under A.R.S. \xa7 33-1321, a security deposit cannot exceed one and a half months' rent. That cap applies to every residential unit, furnished or unfurnished. The deposit must be returned, minus lawful deductions, within 14 business days after the tenant moves out. Elevo does not give legal advice.")
B.bk5=new A.e9("Can I enter my tenant's unit without notice?","Generally no. Under ARS \xa733-1343, you must provide at least 2 days notice before entering a tenant's unit \u2014 except in genuine emergencies. Entry must be at reasonable times. Failure to provide proper notice can constitute a landlord breach of the rental agreement.")
B.bk7=new A.e9("What is the eviction process in Arizona?","Arizona's eviction (Special Detainer) process requires: (1) Written notice to tenant per ARS \xa733-1368; (2) Filing a complaint with Justice Court after notice period expires; (3) A hearing typically within 3\u20136 business days of filing; (4) Writ of Restitution if landlord prevails. Elevo does not give legal advice. Check the statute or a lawyer for your own case.")
B.aSa=s([B.bkm,B.bk5,B.bk7],t.zX)
B.bjX=new A.hL("Arizona Law",B.a67,B.aSa)
B.Ic=s([B.bk1,B.bjZ,B.bjT,B.bjV,B.bk0,B.bjX],t.hm)
B.a3J=new A.fN("1. Who this covers",'These terms are between you and ELEVO Property Management LLC ("Elevo", "we"). They cover the Elevo app and the public terms and privacy pages. They take effect on November 21, 2026. Questions go to hello@getelevo.app.')
B.a3Z=new A.fN("2. Who Elevo is for","Elevo is for landlords, tenants, and vendors or contractors. It is built for residential property in Arizona, in the United States. When a landlord adds a property, the state is Arizona and the form does not let them pick another state. You must be at least 18 years old. Elevo is not for children. Sign-up does not ask for a date of birth.")
B.a3N=new A.fN("3. What Elevo does, and what it does not","Elevo is software for tracking rent, repairs, documents, and messages in one place. Elevo is not a party to a lease, a sale, or a repair contract. Elevo does not employ vendors, does not run background checks on them, and does not guarantee their work. A preferred-partner listing can be reviewed before it is shown. That review is not a promise that the vendor is qualified or trustworthy. Elevo does not give legal, tax, or financial advice, including advice about Arizona eviction or lease language. The landlord More screen may show a separate real-estate contact. That person is not Elevo, and Elevo is not your broker.")
B.a3M=new A.fN("4. Rent and deposits","Elevo does not collect, hold, or process rent or security deposits. A landlord lists the ways they prefer to be paid, such as Zelle, Venmo, a bank transfer, a check, or cash. The tenant pays the landlord directly, outside Elevo. When a tenant taps I Have Paid, and when a landlord confirms that payment, Elevo only saves a record. That record is not a payment, and it does not prove the money moved.")
B.a3X=new A.fN("5. Landlord plans","Landlords can pay Elevo for a plan. The prices on the subscription screen are: Essential, $39.99 a month or $299 a year; Unlimited, $79 a month or $699 a year; Done for You setup, $249 once; an extra property on Essential, $12.99 a month. Essential is 1 property. Each extra property is $12.99 a month. Unlimited has no property limit while the subscription is active. Tenants are not charged to use Elevo. After you confirm your email, you choose Essential or Unlimited before the landlord app opens. That choice opens Stripe and collects a card. The card is not charged that day. It is charged automatically when the 7-day trial ends unless you cancel first. After that, Stripe renews the plan until you cancel. Manage Subscription opens the Stripe billing portal, where you can change the card or cancel. When the trial date has passed and there is no paying plan, or when Stripe marks the subscription past due, canceled, unpaid, or incomplete, Elevo blocks adding another property. Everything already saved stays readable. Deleting an Elevo account turns off the login and clears the contact details. It does not remove a property, unit, or payment instruction other people still need. Deleting the account cancels the Stripe subscription immediately. There is no refund for the current period. Done for You, as the app describes it, is a one-time setup of properties, documents, tenant invitations, and a one-hour onboarding call. The app says Elevo will reach out within one business day after you pay. A landlord can share one referral code. A new landlord may enter that code. Both then receive 20% off for 3 months. The new landlord still adds a card for the 7-day trial. The discount applies to the subscription, including after the trial ends.")
B.a3Y=new A.fN("6. Vendor plans","Vendors can pay for a listing. The monthly prices on the vendor plan screen are Basic $39.99, Featured $89.99, Preferred $149, and Platinum $199. The app does not show a yearly vendor price. Choosing a higher plan opens a Stripe checkout page and charges the new price then. Choosing a lower plan asks you to confirm, then opens the Stripe billing portal. Elevo does not change the vendor plan by itself. The screen says a downgrade waits until the end of the billing period, with no refund for unused time. Preferred and Platinum can be marked full. A full plan offers a waitlist and does not charge until a spot is confirmed.")
B.a3S=new A.fN("7. Tenant screening","Screening uses the landlord's own RentSpree account. The landlord saves their RentSpree link in Elevo, and applicants open that link. Elevo is not part of RentSpree and is not affiliated with it. Elevo does not receive or store the RentSpree credit report. The applicant pays RentSpree, not Elevo. Elevo can store notes the landlord types, and the notes box invites a credit score or a concern. Those notes are the landlord's words, not a report from RentSpree. The landlord, not Elevo, is responsible for the Fair Credit Reporting Act and for fair housing laws, including Arizona law.")
B.a3H=new A.fN("8. Your account","You agree to give a current name, email, and phone, and to keep your password to yourself. Elevo emails you a confirmation link, and the account is not ready until you open it. A tenant is not linked to a unit until that email is confirmed. You are responsible for what happens under your account. If you think someone else signed in, email hello@getelevo.app. Elevo does not offer two-factor sign-in.")
B.a3I=new A.fN("9. Your responsibilities","You will follow the law that applies to you, including landlord-tenant law, fair housing law, and any license you need to do repair work. You will not use Elevo to break the law, to harass someone, or to upload a file you have no right to store.")
B.a3W=new A.fN("10. Changes to these terms","We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page will change in the app and on the public terms page. If you keep using Elevo after that date, you agree to the update. We do not send a separate email for every wording change.")
B.a3U=new A.fN("11. Arizona law","These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona and the United States. Disputes are handled in the state or federal courts in Arizona. If you are a consumer, you may also have rights that these terms cannot take away.")
B.a3Q=new A.fN("12. Contact","Email hello@getelevo.app.")
